-------------------------------------------------------------
  icacls <b> /deny "*<SID>:(OI)(CI)(DE,DC,WD,AD,WEA,WA)" /T /C
    -> 41,822 files processed, 0 failed
  exec probe   <java> -version                     exit 0
  write probe  [IO.File]::WriteAllText(<b>\konan-data\wt.tmp)   denied
  append probe [IO.File]::AppendAllText(<b>\...\.extracted)     denied
  compile with KONAN_DATA_DIR=<b>\konan-data       exit 2
    Details: Internal error in file lowering: java.io.IOException: Access denied
  NOTE, and it is why obligation K-11 exists: an earlier form of the same ACE,
  icacls ... /deny "...(W,D,DC)", denied SYNCHRONIZE as part of the simple
  right W and made java.exe unrunnable ("Access is denied" on process start).
  And with the corrected ACE a delete of a bundle file still SUCCEEDED, because
  the same account holds Full Control through BUILTIN\Administrators, which
  grants FILE_DELETE_CHILD on the parent directory. A per-user deny is not
  sufficient; the bundle must be owned by an account the manager does not run
  as.

